{"slug":"ops-npm-rollback-playbook","title":"Rollback playbook — npm + git","blocks":[{"id":"b1","type":"ingress","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Scope:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" npm rollbacks + git revert for "},{"type":"text","value":"@barkpark/*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and unscoped "},{"type":"text","value":"create-barkpark-app","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"text","value":"NOT covered:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Phoenix/Caddy/DNS rollback (ops-prod-ops, ops-vercel-dns-connect) — deliberately separate runbooks (different blast radii + approvers). Owner: Subtaskmaster; Boss approves unpublish + dist-tag runs."}]},{"id":"b2","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Decision tree"},{"id":"b3","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Symptom"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Window"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Severity"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Mechanism"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"Type-only regression ("},{"type":"text","value":".d.mts","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" breaks "},{"type":"text","value":"tsc","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", runtime works)"}],[{"type":"text","value":"any"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Medium"}],[{"type":"text","value":"deprecate + patch","marks":["strong"]}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime regression — install works, app breaks"}],[{"type":"text","value":"any"}],[{"type":"text","value":"High"}],[{"type":"text","value":"deprecate + patch","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"text","value":"unpublish","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" only if patch > 4h away AND <72h"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Install-time failure"}],[{"type":"text","value":"<72h"}],[{"type":"text","value":"High"}],[{"type":"text","value":"unpublish + patch","marks":["strong"]}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Install-time failure"}],[{"type":"text","value":"≥72h"}],[{"type":"text","value":"High"}],[{"type":"text","value":"deprecate + patch","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (unpublish blocked by policy)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Security (credential leak, RCE, auth bypass)"}],[{"type":"text","value":"any"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Critical","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"unpublish immediately","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (within 72h) + patched release + public CVE"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Accidental debug/scratch publish"}],[{"type":"text","value":"<72h"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Low"}],[{"type":"text","value":"unpublish","marks":["strong"]}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Wrong dist-tag ("},{"type":"text","value":"@latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" at a broken build)"}],[{"type":"text","value":"any"}],[{"type":"text","value":"High"}],[{"type":"text","value":"dist-tag reassign","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (no unpublish)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Wrong tarball contents entirely"}],[{"type":"text","value":"<72h"}],[{"type":"text","value":"High"}],[{"type":"text","value":"unpublish","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":", re-publish at the NEXT version"}]]]},{"id":"b4","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Default to ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"npm deprecate","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":". Reach for ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"npm unpublish","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" only when install is broken for users who would otherwise get the bad version.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Deprecate is reversible (deprecate with "},{"type":"text","value":"\"\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" to undo), non-destructive (version stays installable; pinned users unaffected), visible at install time. Unpublish is "},{"type":"text","value":"irreversible","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" past the first re-publish attempt, breaks every lockfile pinned to that version, and is allowed only within "},{"type":"text","value":"72h","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" of publish ("},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.npmjs.com/policies/unpublish","children":[{"type":"text","value":"npm unpublish policy"}]},{"type":"text","value":"); beyond 72h requires a registry support ticket. Same rule for scoped + unscoped."}]},{"id":"b5","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Mechanism A — npm deprecate (soft recall)"},{"id":"b6","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"For buggy-but-installable versions with a patch landing soon."}]},{"id":"b7","type":"code","value":"npm deprecate @barkpark/core@1.0.0 \"broken types — upgrade to 1.0.1\""},{"id":"b8","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Un-deprecate with message "},{"type":"text","value":"\"\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; ranges work ("},{"type":"text","value":"\"@barkpark/core@<1.0.1\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). Verify: "},{"type":"text","value":"npm view @barkpark/core@1.0.0 deprecated","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" prints the message; version still listed; a scratch install prints "},{"type":"text","value":"npm WARN deprecated","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". If the version is completely uninstallable the warning is never seen — escalate to B."}]},{"id":"b9","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Mechanism B — npm unpublish (hard recall)"},{"id":"b10","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Only for: completely broken installs; security hazards where the artifact itself is the harm; accidental wrong-content publishes caught <72h."}]},{"id":"b11","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Constraints: "},{"type":"text","value":"72h window","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"E403","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" after); blocked if another public package depended on the version in the last 72h; token needs publish + unpublish scope (post-2024 automation tokens default publish-only; 2FA device handy — unscoped packages may require account confirmation)."}]},{"id":"b12","type":"code","value":"npm unpublish @barkpark/core@1.0.0 --force # --force required; unscoped same syntax"},{"id":"b13","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify: "},{"type":"text","value":"npm view @barkpark/core@1.0.0 version","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" → 404; version gone from "},{"type":"text","value":"versions --json","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; check "},{"type":"text","value":"dist-tags --json","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and reassign any tag pointing at the dead version BEFORE or IMMEDIATELY AFTER unpublish."}]},{"id":"b14","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Re-publish blocker (critical):","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" after unpublishing "},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" you "},{"type":"text","value":"cannot publish a new artifact at ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" for 24h","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (registry anti-replay). Always ship the fix as "},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — never re-use the number. This is why deprecate is the default: it doesn't burn a version."}]},{"id":"b15","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Downstream impact:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" every lockfile pinned to the version fails next "},{"type":"text","value":"npm ci","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; pre-write a pinned GitHub issue comment with the upgrade line; CI metadata caches can serve the old manifest for up to 1h. Clear CI caches after any unpublish."}]},{"id":"b16","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Mechanism C — npm dist-tag rollback (reassign @latest)"},{"id":"b17","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"When the artifact is fine but "},{"type":"text","value":"@latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" points at the wrong version."}]},{"id":"b18","type":"code","value":"npm dist-tag add @barkpark/core@0.9.5 latest # move back to last good"},{"id":"b19","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Instant, non-destructive, burns no version number. Prefer over unpublish when the bug is \"wrong version got promoted.\""}]},{"id":"b20","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Dist-tag changes via CI (retag.yml) — absorbed retag runbook"},{"id":"b21","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Local "},{"type":"text","value":"npm dist-tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"text","value":"HTTP 403","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — only the CI "},{"type":"text","value":"NPM_TOKEN","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" holds publish/dist-tag scope on the "},{"type":"text","value":"@barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" org. Dispatch through "},{"type":"text","value":".github/workflows/retag.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"workflow_dispatch","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", on "},{"type":"text","value":"main","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" only; fails fast with "},{"type":"text","value":"::error title=Missing NPM_TOKEN::","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" if the secret is unset). The protected-channel guard refuses "},{"type":"text","value":"remove_tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" of "},{"type":"text","value":"preview","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"text","value":"next","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Reference incident: "},{"type":"text","value":"release.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" run "},{"type":"text","value":"24627335562","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (2026-04-19) published two "},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0-preview.1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" packages to "},{"type":"text","value":"latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" instead of "},{"type":"text","value":"preview","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — see adr-0002-npm-dist-tag-publish."}]},{"id":"b22","type":"callout","tone":"warn","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Approval gate (P0 guardrail):","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"Boss must approve each ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"workflow_dispatch","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" run separately before it executes.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Two packages = two approvals; a re-run after a failure = a fresh approval. Dist-tag changes are immediately live for every npm consumer — the approval cadence is the only human gate."}]},{"id":"b23","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Split-state rollback (run 1 succeeded, run 2 failed):","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" re-run "},{"type":"text","value":"only run 2","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" with the same inputs — the "},{"type":"text","value":"Add dist-tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" step is idempotent on npm. Full undo (restore the version to "},{"type":"text","value":"latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"): dispatch with "},{"type":"text","value":"add_tag=latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"text","value":"remove_tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"empty","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — never strip "},{"type":"text","value":"preview","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on the way back (the guard refuses it anyway). If the workflow cannot start (token missing, not on "},{"type":"text","value":"main","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"), fix the gating and re-dispatch — never improvise locally (403s)."}]},{"id":"b24","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"404-is-intentional:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"npm dist-tag rm <pkg> latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"deletes","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" the "},{"type":"text","value":"latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" entry — it does not reassign. With no stable version published, a bare "},{"type":"text","value":"npm install @barkpark/core","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" then "},{"type":"text","value":"404s","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":". This is the intended interim state: fail-loud beats silently serving a pre-release on the stable channel. The 404 persists until the first stable GA publish; "},{"type":"text","value":"@preview","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" installs and explicit pins are unaffected."}]},{"id":"b25","type":"callout","tone":"info","content":[{"type":"text","value":"ADR divergence note:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" ADR 0002 §Consequences suggests "},{"type":"text","value":"not","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" stripping "},{"type":"text","value":"latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" mid-incident. The incident response deliberately "},{"type":"text","value":"cleared","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (fail-loud). To reassert the ADR posture: dispatch "},{"type":"text","value":"add_tag=preview","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"remove_tag=","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" empty."}]},{"id":"b26","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Mechanism D — git revert (fix the source)"},{"id":"b27","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Every npm rollback is a stopgap; the permanent fix is a revert shipped as a new patch: "},{"type":"text","value":"git revert <bad-sha>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on main → "},{"type":"text","value":"pnpm changeset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (patch) → push → CI publishes. If the revert conflicts, abort and either revert the follow-ups too or forward-fix. "},{"type":"text","value":"Never","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" force-push main to paper over a revert. Don't revert a whole multi-concern PR — undo just the broken piece. npm-side rollback runs in parallel, not after."}]},{"id":"b28","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Incident checklist"},{"id":"b29","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Detect","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (<30 min): GitHub Issues / Uptime Kuma / beta channel; acknowledge in "},{"type":"text","value":"#incidents","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Assess","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (<15 min): reproduce in a scratch dir; classify (type-only / runtime / install-time / security / dist-tag); estimate blast radius."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Decide:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" use the decision tree; "},{"type":"text","value":"write the decision down","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" in the incident ticket before acting. Critical ⇒ Boss approves."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Execute:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" most incidents combine two mechanisms (A+D, C+D, or B+D). Every command goes in the ticket verbatim with timestamps."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Verify:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" mechanism checks above + fresh-install invariant: "},{"type":"text","value":"npx create-barkpark-app@latest blog /tmp/rollback-smoke-$(date +%s)","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Re-test from a clean cache ("},{"type":"text","value":"npm cache clean --force","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Communicate:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" \"rolled back\" banner on the GitHub Release; reply where users reported it."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Postmortem (48h):","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" record as a task in the task system — a "},{"type":"text","value":"type:\"task\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" document via the standard mutate endpoint with "},{"type":"text","value":"content.kind == \"task\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; there is no "},{"type":"text","value":"POST /v1/tasks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" create verb ("},{"type":"text","value":"bp task","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" verbs are read/lifecycle only). Capture timeline, detection gap, decision rationale, fix, prevention. Long-form: attach a Bulldocs paper via "},{"type":"text","value":"POST /v1/tasks/<task_id>/papers","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Never write to "},{"type":"text","value":".doey/plans/","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (archived to "},{"type":"text","value":"_attic","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). File preventive tickets; a same-class second incident upgrades prevention to P0."}]]},{"id":"b30","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Known pitfalls"},{"id":"b31","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"npm deprecate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" does NOT update lockfiles","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — pinned users keep the bad version until they update; communicate via release notes."}],[{"type":"text","value":"GitHub Packages mirror","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — we don't mirror; if we ever do, unpublish doesn't propagate."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Signed tags don't auto-revert","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — delete + re-create the tag after the revert lands, if the tag is load-bearing."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Concurrent "},{"type":"text","value":"changeset publish","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" → E409; wait 30s and retry — don't unpublish the half-failed one."}]]},{"id":"b32","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Drill cadence"},{"id":"b33","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Drill "},{"type":"text","value":"at least once before GA","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"; annually after, sooner on on-call change:"}]},{"id":"b34","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Publish "},{"type":"text","value":"@barkpark/core@0.0.0-rollback-drill-<timestamp>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"text","value":"@preview","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecate within 5 min."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Unpublish within 60 min (inside 72h window)."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Record the drill as a task (same task-system mechanics as the postmortem step): timestamps for published/deprecated/unpublished, observed deviations, labels "},{"type":"text","value":"[\"rollback-drill\", \"ops\"]","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]]}],"related":["ops-prod-ops","ops-vercel-dns-connect","adr-0002-npm-dist-tag-publish"]}
